course: dictionary
lesson: 10291
title: Total: the whole amount
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word total can do several jobs. As a noun, it is the whole amount you get when you add everything up. «Together the two amounts are 1 + 3 = 4 units, so one unit is the total divided by 4.» Here the total is 4, the answer after adding.
explain: As an adjective, total means whole or complete. «Total silence» means there is no sound at all, not even a little. Check the words around it to see which job the word has.
explain: As a verb, to total means to add up to an amount. «The bill totals 20 dollars» means that when you add everything on the bill, the answer is 20 dollars. You may also see totals, totalled and totaled.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. If «complete» fits in «total silence» and still makes sense, you have found the right meaning. If you are stuck, use a dictionary.
fact: Total means the whole amount when you add everything up.
fact: «Total silence» means complete silence, with no sound at all.
fact: «A running total» is a total that keeps growing as you add each new number.
fact: In formal writing, total can be replaced by words such as sum or aggregate, as in «the sum total».
fact: «Totally» means completely, as in «totally sure».
exercise: «Some problems take two steps: first multiply to find the total of the equal groups, then add or take away.» What does total mean in this sentence? | The part you take away | The start of the problem | *The whole amount found by adding up | The name of a group
exercise: «The bill totals 20 dollars.» What does totals mean here? | Breaks | Hides | Pays back | *Adds up to
exercise: Which word has the same meaning as total in «total silence»? | *Complete | Loud | Slow | Warm
test: «A microtransaction is a small payment inside a game; many small payments add up to a big total.» What is the big total? | A game with no payments | The start of the game | A small payment only | *The whole amount of all the payments added together
test: «Route-finding algorithms compare many possible roads, add up the time for each, and pick the shortest total.» What does shortest total mean here? | The road with no name | A map with no roads | The longest road | *The least time added up for a whole road
exam: «When food prices go up, the same basket costs more, so a running total in your head stops nasty surprises at the till.» What does running total mean? | A list with no numbers | *A total that keeps growing as you add each item | A total you run away from | A race to the shop
